5,Fungwa language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/fungwa_language,"Fungwa, also known as Ura or Ula, is an endangered Kainji language of the Benue-Congo branch within the Niger-Congo family, spoken by approximately 3,000 to 3,500 people primarily in five villages—G.",Fungwa,Niger-Congo
6,ComparaLex - Fungwa,https://comparalex.org/?w1=182,"Fungwa. Location of idiolect: Niger state, Rafi LGA. Country: Nigeria. ISO 639-3 code: ula (more info at ethnologue.com). Standard list used for elicitation: Benue-Congo Comparative Word List. Words",Fungwa,Niger-Congo
7,(PDF) Featural affixation and sound symbolism in Fungwa,https://www.researchgate.net/publication/358764846_Featural_affixation_and_sound_symbolism_in_Fungwa,"Fungwa is a Kainji (Benue-Congo) language with about 1000 speakers. (Blench 2018, Eberhard et al. 2019). The language is spoken in at least. thirteen villages along Pandogari-Alawa Road in RaﬁLocal Government, Niger State, Nigeria. Like most Kainji languages, Fungwa is endangered.",Fungwa,Niger-Congo
